      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{-2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{-3}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =-6{x}^{-3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
